## Refresh tokens

`POST /auth/refresh` with `{refresh_token}` returns a new pair. Each refresh
token works once; the response carries the next one. They are random strings
stored as SHA-256 hashes, valid `REFRESH_TOKEN_DAYS` (30).

Every token of one sign-in is a *family*. A token presented again after it
was traded means a copy exists, so the whole family is revoked: thief and user
both sign in again, and a `refresh_token_reused` event is logged. One
consequence: an app that sends the same refresh twice at once (two requests
racing after a 401) signs itself out, so refresh from one place in the app.

`POST /auth/logout` revokes the family of the token it is sent.
